Per #2, the use of `dplyr::c_across()` creates a requirement for the use of dplyr 1.0.0 or later. A lot of our target environments could very well still be using pre 1.0.0 versions so it's well worth it to eliminate the  single line that creates this dependency. 

@statasaurus let me know if you see any issue with this solution. I tried to preserve your methodology of using `c_across()` and make sure the solution is functionally the same. So for this line, any column that beings with `where` will be concatenated and delimited with a space.

All existing tests pass. R CMD check passes as well.

Moved to the latest TileDB and fixed issue with vidmap generation. There should only be one type for fields(e.g. DP) that exist as both INFO and FORMAT. 

```
 {
   "name": "DP",
   "type": [
    "Integer"
   ],
   "vcf_field_class": [
    "FORMAT",
    "INFO"
   ],
   "length": [
    {
     "variable_length_descriptor": "1"
    }
   ]
  }
```

There is [support for vcf_name](https://github.com/GenomicsDB/GenomicsDB/blob/d59e886a5351ffc68b58758bc14f61025d2fa833/src/resources/genomicsdb_vid_mapping.proto#L51) in the protobuf definition. @kgururaj, would this be the way to go?

